Coinbase sets Friday deadline for Europeans still holding USDT

@coinbase will convert balances of 14 stablecoins held by retail customers in the European Economic Area on Friday, Oct 30. Their issuers lack approval under the EU’s MiCA rules, whose grace period ended July 1. The list includes Tether’s $USDT, PayPal’s PYUSD, World Liberty Financial's USD1, DAI, and PAXG.

Holdings will switch to $USDC, or another supported asset where USDC doesn’t fit, unless users move them to an outside wallet first. Coins sent to Coinbase after the deadline won’t be credited, and getting them back isn’t guaranteed.

